id: rule-while-bad
title: A bad invariant
topic: Loop
example-of: WHILE
derived: false

task:
  Use the rule WHILE to try to derive this triple. The conclusion of the
  rule has the invariant $I$ as precondition, so the candidate invariant
  is the precondition $x > 0$.

given:
  Loop condition B: $x > 0$

pre: x > 0
post: x > 0 && !(x > 0)

scheme: WHILE
  Preservation: {«I» && «x > 0 : B»} x := x - 1 {«I»}
  ---
  {«I»} while x > 0 do x := x - 1 {«I» && «!(x > 0) : ¬B»}

program:
  {P}
  {I}
  while x > 0 do {
    {I && x > 0}
    {R1}
    x := x - 1     // b
    {I}
  }
  {I && !(x > 0)}
  {Q}

verdict: invalid

step: The candidate invariant I
rule: WHILE
focus: while
text:
  The rule WHILE uses the precondition of its conclusion as the
  invariant.
set: I = x > 0

step: P implies I
part: Initialisation
rule: CONSEQUENCE
focus: P, I
text:
  >>> «P» ==> «I»
vc: x > 0 ==> x > 0
why:
  $P$ and $I$ are the same formula.

step: R1, the weakest precondition of the body for I
part: Preservation
rule: ASSIGN
focus: b
text:
  One iteration must keep the invariant:
  >>> {«I» && «x > 0 : B»} x := x - 1 {«I»}
  We substitute the variable $x$ with $x - 1$ in $I$.
calc:
  wp(x := x - 1, I)
  = (x > 0)[x <- x - 1]     // I is x > 0
  = x - 1 > 0               // x replaced by x - 1
  = x > 1                   // add 1 to both sides
set: R1 = x > 1

step: I and B do not imply R1
part: Preservation
rule: CONSEQUENCE
focus: I && x > 0, R1
text:
  >>> «I» && «x > 0 : B» ==> «R1»
vc: x > 0 && x > 0 ==> x > 1
status: fails
counterexample: x = 1
why:
  In the state $x = 1$ the body gives $x = 0$, which does not satisfy $I$.
  The last iteration always leaves the candidate, so it is not an
  invariant, and the rule cannot be applied.

step: I and not B imply Q
part: Conclusion
rule: CONSEQUENCE
focus: I && !(x > 0), Q
text:
  >>> «I» && «!(x > 0) : ¬B» ==> «Q»
vc: x > 0 && !(x > 0) ==> x > 0 && !(x > 0)
why:
  This premise holds, since $Q$ is $I && !B$, but preservation failed.
  The postcondition is $false$, and the loop does stop, so the triple is
  not valid.
